A.AA=s(["umrkosh carries two kinds of information and never mixes them. The chilling-injury flags and the do-not-stack pairs come from one named book and are printed with their source. The holding days are yours: nothing in this app knows how long anything lasts on your cart, in your season, under your cloth.","Agriculture Handbook 66 is a commercial cold-storage handbook written for controlled rooms in another country. umrkosh ships none of its storage temperatures, humidities or shelf-life figures \u2014 not as a column, not as a tooltip, not in the data, not inside a citation. A cart is not a cold room, and quoting those numbers here would borrow authority this app has not earned.","A chilling-injury flag is about the commodity, not about your fridge. Whether damage actually happens depends on how cold, for how long and how ripe. The handbook records that the injury exists; it is not a guarantee about your ice box.",'"No chilling injury recorded" does not mean "keep it cold." It means the handbook did not list an injury. umrkosh has no value that means "safe to refrigerate", and it will never tell you to chill anything.',"Ethylene pairing is a rate, not a switch. A producer next to a sensitive item makes it ripen and yellow faster. It does not ruin it instantly, and separating them does not stop ripening.","Cultivars and conditions differ. Handbook rows are commodity-level. Your variety, your season, your day\u2019s heat and how the load was handled can all move the answer.",'Some things families sell every day are simply not in this handbook, and some that are in it carry no sentence we could quote for one of the two facts. Those are two different silences and umrkosh names them separately \u2014 "not in Handbook 66 at all" and "in Handbook 66, but no sentence to quote" \u2014 rather than merging them or guessing.',"The holding days are not advice and not a prediction. They are your own number, applied by subtraction. If your sheet is empty, umrkosh sorts nothing and says so.","umrkosh is not a food-safety app. It says nothing about whether anything is safe to eat. If it looks wrong or smells wrong, throw it out whatever any chart says.","Local-first: your data is a SQLite file on your machine; the app runs on localhost; nothing syncs anywhere, there are no accounts and no encryption. The demo stores nothing server-side."],t.s)
